# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 211-215 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 16 — CHAPTERS 19-21, LEAN, 2026-09-24; RUN 2 — the portion edge at 21:9|21:10, 211 heads on
# 21:10): the optional war, against not with, the promise, the Canaanites within, at the time of captivity, even a married woman, even ugly, not for the father
# or brother (211); into his house not another's, R. Eliezer trims and R. Akiva grows the nails, the two "doing"s, Mephibosheth's proof (212); the captive's
# garb to widow's garb, the house he uses, the parents actual or idols, a month of days thirty or three months, R. Eliezer's why, the acts before the
# consummation, only the commandment of consummation, Exodus 21:10's three (213); the verse announces the hatred, not to her god's house, the bill and the
# sick woman, no gift or favor, no use, after a single act (214); "wives" the legitimate marriages, R. Ishmael's way of the world, the doubt of nine and seven,
# the side-birth, more than two, all loved or all hated, even one, the hated before the Omnipresent — the forbidden marriages by the redundancy, the slave-girl
# and the gentile excluded, sons not daughters, not the tumtum, not the doubt, the firstborn to the hated (215). Every row READ WHOLE; the cuts by
# ch19_ink.SP_. Sitting 15's form.
