srow(211, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU GO OUT TO WAR" (21:10) — THE VERSE SPEAKS OF AN OPTIONAL WAR. ({SP_(211, 1, "במלחמת", "הרשות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "the verse speaks of an optional war"): THE CAPTIVE\'S LAW SCOPED TO THE OPTIONAL WAR (199:1\'s clause verbatim; the seven nations leave no captives, 20:16) — the compile\'s war-kind condition on the captive cell. Fresh.')
srow(211, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" — OPPOSITE YOUR ENEMIES. ({SP_(211, 2, "כנגד", "אויביך")} "opposite your enemies"): the preposition read as opposition, not alliance (the English\'s gloss). Fresh.')
srow(211, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES HIM INTO YOUR HAND" — IF YOU DID ALL THAT IS SAID IN THE MATTER, IN THE END THE LORD GIVES HIM INTO YOUR HAND. ({SP_(211, 3, "אם", "עשית", "כל", "האמור", "בענין")} "if you did all that is said in the matter"; {SP_(211, 3, "סוף", "שה", "אלהיך", "נותנו", "בידך")} "in the end the LORD your God gives him into your hand"): the promise conditioned on the war laws — a narrative reading, no rule. Fresh.')
srow(211, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU CAPTURE ITS CAPTIVES" — TO INCLUDE THE CANAANITES INSIDE IT. ({SP_(211, 4, "לרבות", "כנענים", "שבתוכה")} "to include the Canaanites inside it"): the seven nations\' members found inside a far city may be taken captive (200:2\'s reading on 20:11 the twin) — the compile\'s note on the captive\'s nation. Fresh.')
srow(211, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SEE AMONG THE CAPTIVES" (21:11) — AT THE TIME OF CAPTIVITY. ({SP_(211, 5, "בשעת", "שביה")} "at the time of captivity"): THE DESIRE\'S MOMENT — the battlefield, not later (Kiddushin 21b\'s "the Torah spoke against the evil inclination" in the background) — the compile\'s timing condition. Fresh.')
srow(211, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"A WOMAN" — EVEN THOUGH SHE IS A MARRIED WOMAN. ({SP_(211, 6, "שהיא", "אשת", "איש")} "though she is a married woman"): the captive\'s marital state no bar — the compile\'s note (the gentile marriage not a bond here). Fresh.')
srow(211, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF BEAUTIFUL FORM" — I HAVE ONLY WHEN SHE IS FAIR; WHENCE EVEN UGLY? "AND YOU DESIRE HER" — THOUGH SHE IS NOT OF BEAUTIFUL FORM. ({SP_(211, 7, "בזמן", "שהיא", "נאה")} "when she is fair"; {SP_(211, 7, "מנין", "אפילו", "היא", "כעורה")} "whence even if she is ugly"; {SP_(211, 7, "שאינה", "יפת", "תאר")} "though she is not of beautiful form"): the beauty an example, the desire the condition — the compile\'s condition is the desire. Fresh.')
srow(211, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU TAKE HER FOR YOURSELF AS A WIFE" — THAT YOU NOT SAY: THIS ONE FOR MY FATHER, THIS ONE FOR MY BROTHER. ({SP_(211, 8, "שלא", "תאמר")} "that you not say"; {SP_(211, 8, "הרי", "זו", "לאבה", "הרי", "זו", "לאחי")} "this one for my father, this one for my brother"): THE TAKER IS THE DESIRER — no transfer of the captive to another — the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(212, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU BRING HER INTO YOUR HOUSE" (21:12) — AND NOT INTO ANOTHER HOUSE. ({SP_(212, 1, "ולא", "לבית", "אחר")} "and not into another house"): the month in his own house — the compile\'s place condition. Fresh.')
srow(212, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL SHAVE HER HEAD AND DO HER NAILS" — R. ELIEZER SAYS: SHE CUTS; R. AKIVA SAYS: SHE GROWS. ({SP_(212, 2, "אליעזר", "אומר", "תקוץ")} "Eliezer says: she cuts"; {SP_(212, 2, "עקיבה", "אומר", "תגדל")} "Akiva says: she grows"): THE NAILS\' DISPUTE — Onkelos took R. Akiva\'s growing (21:12 "let her nails grow", the ink\'s find 4; Yevamot 48a) — the compile\'s parameter with the dispute, Onkelos\'s arm marked. Fresh.')
srow(212, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER SAID: "DOING" IS SAID OF THE HEAD AND OF THE NAILS — AS THE HEAD\'S DOING IS REMOVAL, SO THE NAILS\' DOING IS REMOVAL. ({SP_(212, 3, "מה", "עשיה", "האמורה", "בראש", "העברה")} "as the doing said of the head is removal"; {SP_(212, 3, "אף", "עשיה", "האמורה", "בצפרנים", "העברה")} "so the doing said of the nails is removal"): R. Eliezer\'s analogy from the shared verb. Fresh.')
srow(212, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA SAYS: AS THE HEAD\'S DOING IS DISFIGUREMENT, SO THE NAILS\' DOING IS DISFIGUREMENT. AND A PROOF FOR R. ELIEZER: "MEPHIBOSHETH … HAD NOT DONE HIS FEET NOR DONE HIS MOUSTACHE" (2 SAMUEL 19:25). ({SP_(212, 4, "בראש", "נוול")} "of the head, disfigurement"; {SP_(212, 4, "בצפרנים", "נוול")} "of the nails, disfigurement"; {SP_(212, 4, "וראיה", "לדברי", "רבי", "אליעזר")} "and a proof for R. Eliezer\'s words"): R. Akiva\'s purpose-reading (disfigurement) against R. Eliezer\'s word-reading, with Mephibosheth\'s "doing" as trimming for R. Eliezer — the Prophets a case, never a row. Fresh.')
srow(213, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL REMOVE THE GARMENT OF HER CAPTIVITY" (21:13) — HE TAKES OFF HER FINE CLOTHES AND DRESSES HER IN WIDOW\'S GARB, FOR THE NATIONS\' DAUGHTERS ADORN THEMSELVES IN WAR TO WHORE OTHERS AFTER THEM. ({SP_(213, 1, "שמעביר", "ממנה", "בגדים", "נאים")} "that he removes from her fine garments"; {SP_(213, 1, "ומלבישה", "בגדי", "אלמנות")} "and dresses her in widow\'s garments"; {SP_(213, 1, "בנותיהם", "מתקשטות", "במלחמה")} "their daughters adorn themselves in war"): the garment change a disfigurement (Yevamot 48a) — the compile\'s first act of the month. Fresh.')
srow(213, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL DWELL IN YOUR HOUSE" — IN THE HOUSE HE USES: HE STUMBLES ON HER GOING IN AND GOING OUT, AND SEES HER IN HER DISFIGUREMENT. ({SP_(213, 2, "בבית", "שמשתמש", "בו")} "in the house he uses"; {SP_(213, 2, "נתקל", "בה", "ונכנס")} "he stumbles on her going in"; {SP_(213, 2, "ורואה", "בנוולה")} "and sees her disfigurement"): the month\'s purpose — his sight of her disfigured (the compile\'s note: the dwelling in the used house). Fresh.')
srow(213, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL WEEP FOR HER FATHER AND HER MOTHER A MONTH OF DAYS" — HER ACTUAL FATHER AND MOTHER (R. ELIEZER); R. AKIVA: HER FATHER AND MOTHER ARE IDOLATRY — "THEY SAY TO THE WOOD: YOU ARE MY FATHER" (JEREMIAH 2:27). ({SP_(213, 3, "אביה", "ואמה", "ממש")} "her father and her mother literally"; {SP_(213, 3, "אין", "אביה", "ואמה", "אלא", "עבודה", "זרה")} "her father and mother are nothing but idolatry"): the weeping\'s object disputed — the parents or her gods (Yevamot 48b) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(213, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MONTH OF DAYS" — THIRTY DAYS. ANOTHER READING: "A MONTH" ONE, "DAYS" TWO — THREE MONTHS, FOR HER FINE CLOTHES AND HIS DESIRE TO FADE, AND THE CHILD\'S PATERNITY (R. AKIVA), BETWEEN THE FIRST SEED AND THE SECOND. ({SP_(213, 4, "ירח", "ימים", "שלשים", "יום")} "a month of days: thirty days"; {SP_(213, 4, "ירח", "אחד", "ימים", "שנים", "הרי", "שלשה", "חדשים")} "month one, days two: three months"; {SP_(213, 4, "ותקון", "הולד")} "and the child\'s establishment"; {SP_(213, 4, "בין", "זרע", "ראשון", "לזרע", "שני")} "between the first seed and the second"): THE WAIT\'S LENGTH — thirty days, or three months for paternity (the widow\'s three months, Yevamot 4:10) — the compile\'s duration parameter with both readings. Fresh.')
srow(213, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER SAYS: "A MONTH OF DAYS" AS IT SOUNDS; AND WHY ALL THIS? THAT A DAUGHTER OF ISRAEL REJOICE WHILE THIS ONE WEEPS, ADORN HERSELF WHILE THIS ONE IS DISFIGURED. ({SP_(213, 5, "ירח", "ימים", "כמשמעו")} "a month of days as it sounds"; {SP_(213, 5, "שתהא", "בת", "ישראל", "שמחה", "וזו", "בוכה")} "that a daughter of Israel rejoice and this one weep"): R. Eliezer\'s thirty days and the rite\'s purpose (his eye turned to the Israelite). Fresh.')
srow(213, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AFTER THAT YOU MAY COME TO HER AND BE HER HUSBAND" — IF HE DID NOT DO ALL THESE ACTS TO HER AND CAME TO HER, IT IS A CONSUMMATION OF HARLOTRY. ({SP_(213, 6, "הא", "אם", "לא", "עשה", "בה")} "but if he did not do to her"; {SP_(213, 6, "הרי", "זו", "בעילת", "זנות")} "this is a consummation of harlotry"): THE ACTS ARE CONDITIONS OF THE MARRIAGE — the sequence enforced (the compile\'s order: the acts, the month, then the marriage; else the verdict "harlotry"). Fresh.')
srow(213, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AFTER THAT YOU MAY COME TO HER" — YOU HAVE OF HER NOTHING BUT THE COMMANDMENT OF CONSUMMATION. ({SP_(213, 7, "אין", "לך", "בה", "אלא", "מצות", "בעילה")} "you have of her nothing but the commandment of consummation"): the marriage by consummation alone (no other acquisition) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(213, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL BE YOUR WIFE" — AS IT SAYS: "HER FOOD, HER CLOTHING AND HER CONJUGAL RIGHT HE SHALL NOT DIMINISH" (EXODUS 21:10). ({SP_(213, 8, "כענין", "שנאמר")} "as the matter said"; {SP_(213, 8, "שארה", "כסותה", "ועונתה")} "her food, her clothing and her conjugal right"; {SP_(213, 8, "לא", "יגרע")} "he shall not diminish"): THE WIFE\'S THREE DUES from the Hebrew maidservant\'s verse — a REFERENCE to the compiled Exodus 21 cell (the family runner\'s three dues) — the compile\'s CALL edge. Fresh.')
srow(214, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND IF YOU DO NOT DESIRE HER" (21:14) — THE VERSE ANNOUNCES THAT YOU WILL COME TO HATE HER. ({SP_(214, 1, "הכתוב", "מבשרך", "שאתה", "עתיד", "לשנאותה")} "the verse announces to you that you will come to hate her"): the narrative announcement (the chapter\'s chain: the captive, the hated wife, the rebellious son — 218:5) — no rule. Fresh.')
srow(214, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SEND HER TO HERSELF" — AND NOT TO HER GOD\'S HOUSE. ({SP_(214, 2, "ולא", "לבית", "אלהיה")} "and not to the house of her god"): the release not a return to idolatry — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(214, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SEND HER" — WITH A BILL, R. JONATHAN\'S WORDS; AND IF SHE WAS SICK HE WAITS UNTIL SHE RECOVERS — ALL THE MORE FOR THE DAUGHTERS OF ISRAEL, WHO ARE HOLY AND PURE. ({SP_(214, 3, "בגט", "כדברי", "רבי", "יונתן")} "with a bill, as R. Jonathan\'s words"; {SP_(214, 3, "ואם", "היתה", "חולה", "ימתין", "לה", "עד", "שתבריא")} "and if she was sick he waits for her until she recovers"; {SP_(214, 3, "קל", "וחומר", "לבנות", "ישראל")} "all the more for the daughters of Israel"): THE RELEASE IS A DIVORCE (the bill of 24:1 ahead — a pointer forward) and the sick wife waited for — the compile\'s release cell as the divorce\'s, the a-fortiori to Israel\'s daughters. Fresh.')
srow(214, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SURELY NOT SELL HER FOR MONEY" — I HAVE ONLY FOR MONEY; WHENCE NOT AS A GIFT, NOR DO HER A FAVOR? "YOU SHALL SURELY NOT SELL HER FOR MONEY". ({SP_(214, 4, "שלא", "יתננה", "במתנה")} "that he not give her as a gift"; {SP_(214, 4, "ולא", "יעשה", "בה", "טובה")} "and not do a favor with her"): the sale bar widened to any transfer by the doubled verb — the compile\'s status "not transferable". Fresh.')
srow(214, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT DEAL WITH HER AS A SLAVE" — YOU SHALL NOT MAKE USE OF HER. ANOTHER READING: AS R. JONATHAN. ANOTHER: A WARNING TO THE COURT. ({SP_(214, 5, "שלא", "תשתמש", "בה")} "that you not make use of her"; {SP_(214, 5, "הרי", "זו", "אזהרה", "לבית", "דין")} "this is a warning to the court"): the enslaving bar and its addressee (the court a third reading, 221:10\'s trope) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(214, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BECAUSE YOU HAVE HUMBLED HER" — EVEN AFTER A SINGLE ACT. ({SP_(214, 6, "אפלו", "לאחר", "מעשה", "יחידי")} "even after a single act"): one consummation triggers the bars — the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(215, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MAN HAS TWO WIVES" (21:15) — WHO HAVE MARRIAGE IN THEM; OUT GO THE SLAVE-GIRL AND THE GENTILE, WHO HAVE NO MARRIAGE. MIGHT THIS EXCLUDE THE LEVIRATE WIDOW AND THE BETROTHED? "TWO WIVES". ({SP_(215, 1, "שיש", "בהם", "הויה")} "who have marriage in them"; {SP_(215, 1, "יצאו", "שפחה", "ונכרית")} "out go the slave-girl and the gentile"; {SP_(215, 1, "את", "היבמה", "ומוציא", "את", "הארוסה")} "the levirate widow, and excludes the betrothed"): THE WIVES ARE LEGITIMATE MARRIAGES — the slave-girl\'s and the gentile\'s sons no heirs; the widow\'s and the betrothed\'s kept — the compile\'s wife-class condition on the firstborn cell (the family runner\'s marriage statuses). Fresh.')
srow(215, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ISHMAEL SAYS: THE VERSE SPEAKS OF THE WAY OF THE WORLD; IT TELLS THAT IN THE END HE HATES ONE AND LOVES ANOTHER. ({SP_(215, 2, "בדרך", "ארץ", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "the verse speaks of the way of the world"; {SP_(215, 2, "שסופו", "להיות", "שונא", "אותה", "ואוהב", "אחרת")} "that in the end he hates her and loves another"): the two wives\' narrative (Lamech\'s phrase, Leah\'s word — the ink\'s find 10) — no rule (the row without a citation). Fresh.')
srow(215, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY BEAR HIM SONS" — TO EXCLUDE THE DOUBT: A NINE-MONTH CHILD OF THE FIRST, A SEVEN-MONTH CHILD OF THE LATTER. ({SP_(215, 3, "להוציא", "את", "הספק")} "to exclude the doubt"; {SP_(215, 3, "בן", "תשעה", "לראשון", "בן", "שבעה", "לאחרון")} "a son of nine to the first, a son of seven to the latter"): THE DOUBTFUL FIRSTBORN TAKES NOTHING (215:15 restates) — the widow who remarried within three months (213:4\'s clock) — the compile\'s doubt condition. Fresh.')
srow(215, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY ONE WHO COMES OUT FROM THE PLACE OF BIRTH; ONE BORN BY THE SIDE WHENCE? "AND THEY BEAR HIM" — IN ANY WAY. ({SP_(215, 4, "היוצא", "ממקום", "הלידה")} "who comes out from the place of birth"; {SP_(215, 4, "יוצא", "דפן", "מנין")} "one who comes out of the side, whence"; {SP_(215, 4, "מכל", "מקום")} "in any way"): the side-born son inherits double (Bekhorot 8:2 disputes this for the firstborn\'s portion — the English silent; the compile notes the Mishnah\'s exclusion as the answer sheet\'s) — the compile\'s birth-manner parameter, the Sifrei\'s reading. Fresh.')
srow(215, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER READING: "WHEN A MAN HAS TWO WIVES" — I HAVE ONLY TWO; WHENCE EVEN MANY? "WIVES". ({SP_(215, 5, "אין", "לי", "אלא", "שהן", "שתים")} "I have only that they are two"; {SP_(215, 5, "מנין", "אפלו", "הן", "מרבות")} "whence even if they are many"): the two an example — the compile\'s count unbounded. Fresh.')
srow(215, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY MANY, SOME LOVED AND SOME HATED; WHENCE ALL LOVED OR ALL HATED? "LOVED — THE LOVED; HATED — THE HATED": THE VERSE INCLUDED. ({SP_(215, 6, "ומקצתן", "אהובות", "ומקצתן", "שנואות")} "some loved and some hated"; {SP_(215, 6, "אפלו", "כלן", "אהובות", "כלן", "שנואות")} "even all loved, all hated"; {SP_(215, 6, "אהובה", "האהובה", "שנואה", "השנואה", "רבה", "הכתוב")} "loved, the loved; hated, the hated — the verse included"): the doubled adjectives (the article\'s repetition) widen the case — the love and hatred no conditions. Fresh.')
srow(215, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY MANY, ALL LOVED OR ALL HATED; WHENCE EVEN TWO? "TWO WIVES". ({SP_(215, 7, "וכלן", "אהובות", "או", "כלן", "שנואות")} "and all loved or all hated"; {SP_(215, 7, "מנין", "אפלו", "הן", "שתים")} "whence even two"; {SP_(215, 7, "שתי", "נשים")} "two wives"): the ladder back to two. Fresh.')
srow(215, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY TWO, ONE LOVED AND ONE HATED; WHENCE EVEN ONE, LOVED OR HATED? "LOVED — LOVED; HATED — HATED": THE VERSE INCLUDED. ({SP_(215, 8, "אחת", "אהובה", "ואחת", "שנואה")} "one loved and one hated"; {SP_(215, 8, "אפלו", "אחת", "והיא", "אהובה")} "even one and she is loved"; {SP_(215, 8, "אהובה", "אהובה", "שנואה", "שנואה", "רבה", "הכתוב")} "loved, loved; hated, hated — the verse included"): THE FIRSTBORN\'S DOUBLE HOLDS WITH ONE WIFE — the two wives no condition at all (the ladder\'s end) — the compile\'s cell keyed on the firstborn, not the wives. Fresh.')
srow(215, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'WHICH IS "LOVED"? LOVED BEFORE THE OMNIPRESENT; "HATED"? HATED BEFORE THE OMNIPRESENT. I HAVE ONLY THE RAPED AND THE SEDUCED; WHENCE A WIDOW TO A HIGH PRIEST, A DIVORCEE OR A HALUTZAH (THE RELEASED WIDOW) TO A COMMON PRIEST? "HATED — HATED": IT INCLUDED THE FORBIDDEN UNIONS UNDER A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(215, 9, "אהובה", "לפני", "המקום")} "loved before the Omnipresent"; {SP_(215, 9, "אנוסה", "ומפתה")} "the raped and the seduced"; {SP_(215, 9, "אלמנה", "לכהן", "גדול", "גרושה", "וחלוצה", "לכהן", "הדיוט")} "a widow to a high priest, a divorcee and a released widow to a common priest"; {SP_(215, 9, "רבה", "את", "העריות", "שהן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "it included the forbidden unions that are under a prohibition"): THE HATRED IS HEAVEN\'S — the forbidden marriage\'s son is a firstborn (Yevamot 2:5\'s principle: the son of a forbidden union inherits) — the compile\'s marriage-class table: the prohibited unions counted. Fresh.')
srow(215, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'AND STILL NOT THE UNIONS LIABLE TO EXCISION BY HEAVEN? "HATED — HATED": INCLUDED. AND STILL NOT THOSE LIABLE TO DEATH BY THE COURT? "HATED — HATED": INCLUDED. ({SP_(215, 10, "כרת", "בידי", "שמים")} "excision by the hands of Heaven"; {SP_(215, 10, "מיתת", "בית", "דין")} "death by the court"): the ladder to the gravest unions — every son of an Israelite union a firstborn for the double (the mamzer included) — the compile\'s table complete. Fresh.')
srow(215, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN A SLAVE-GIRL, EVEN A GENTILE? "WHEN A MAN HAS" — ONE WHO HAS MARRIAGE IN THEM; OUT GO THESE WHO HAVE NO MARRIAGE. ({SP_(215, 11, "יכול", "אפלו", "שפחה", "אפלו", "נכרית")} "might even a slave-girl, even a gentile"; {SP_(215, 11, "מי", "שיש", "לו", "בהן", "הויה")} "one who has marriage in them"): the bottom of the ladder — the two unions with no marriage excluded (215:1 restated). Fresh.')
srow(215, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY BEAR HIM SONS" — WHOSE CHILDREN ARE HIS; OUT GO THESE WHOSE CHILDREN ARE NOT HIS. ({SP_(215, 12, "מי", "שהולדות", "שלו")} "one whose children are his"; {SP_(215, 12, "יצאו", "אלו", "שאין", "הולדות", "שלו")} "out go these whose children are not his"): the slave-girl\'s and the gentile\'s children follow the mother (Kiddushin 3:12) — the compile\'s lineage rule referenced. Fresh.')
srow(215, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER READING: "AND THEY BEAR HIM SONS" — SONS ARE IN THIS LAW, DAUGHTERS ARE NOT. SINCE DAUGHTERS ENTER THE INHERITANCE IN THE BROTHERS\' PLACE TO DIVIDE EQUALLY, MIGHT THE FIRSTBORN\'S RIGHT APPLY TO THEM? "SONS". ({SP_(215, 13, "הבנים", "בתורה", "הזאת", "ואין", "הבנות")} "sons are in this law and not daughters"; {SP_(215, 13, "שהבנות", "נכנסות", "לנחלה", "תחת", "האחים")} "that daughters enter the inheritance in the brothers\' place"; {SP_(215, 13, "יכול", "תהא", "בכורה", "נוהגת", "בהן")} "might the firstborn\'s right apply to them"): NO FIRSTBORN DAUGHTER — Numbers 27\'s daughters inherit but take no double (Bava Batra 8:4) — the compile\'s sex condition, the inheritance cell of Numbers 27 REFERENCED. Fresh.')
srow(215, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE SON SHALL BE" — AND NOT A TUMTUM (THE SEALED) OR AN ANDROGYNOS (THE TWO-SEXED). ({SP_(215, 14, "ולא", "טמטום", "ואנדרוגינוס")} "and not a tumtum or an androgynos"): the doubtful sexes no firstborn (Bava Batra 8:2\'s pair) — the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(215, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FIRSTBORN" — AND NOT THE DOUBTFUL. ({SP_(215, 15, "הבכור", "ולא", "הספק")} "the firstborn and not the doubtful"): 215:3\'s doubt restated on the noun. Fresh.')
srow(215, 16, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO THE HATED" — THE VERSE ANNOUNCES THAT THE FIRSTBORN SON IS THE HATED WIFE\'S. ({SP_(215, 16, "הכתוב", "מבשרך", "שבן", "הבכור", "לשניאה")} "the verse announces that the firstborn son is the hated one\'s"): the narrative announcement (Leah\'s Reuben) — no rule. Fresh.')
